## 3.3. Ions in water bodies
Actual wastewater contains organic components (mainly organic matter) and various ions that can affect the performance of the catalyst in a photo-Fenton system through various routes, including modulating $\mathsf{p H}$ , trapping free radicals, and/or affecting the decomposition of $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}$ . Most cations have no effect on the reaction, and some metal cations that react with $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}$ promote the activation of the Fenton reagent to improve degradation. However, anions occupy the active sites on the catalyst surface and act as scavengers for free radicals, competing with them for the active material, thus affecting the efficiency of the photo-Fenton reaction. Xu et al. [102] prepared $\mathrm{\alpha_{\mathrm{(\alpha-Fe_{2}O_{3}}}}$ using benzimidazole (BIm)- modified Fe-MOFs as templates, and found that $\mathbf{Cl}^{-}$ and $\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$ had the highest effect among the co-existing ions $(\mathbf{Cl}^{-}$ , ${\mathsf{N O}}_{3}{}^{-}$ , $\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$ , and $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{PO}_{4}^{-})$ on the $\mathrm{\bf{\alpha}}_{\mathrm{{\tiny{(d-Fe_{2}}\mathrm{{O}}_{3}}}}$ photo-Fenton degradation of MB. For $\mathbf{Cl}^{-}$ , this can be attributed to its ability to serve as a sink for OH to produce less reactive chloride radical anions (Eqs. (11) and (12)). The MB removal rate was only $11\%$ within $40\mathrm{min}$ in the presence of $10\mathrm{mMHCO_{3}^{-}}$ . These results indicate that $\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$ acted as a scavenger to quench •OH [127] and increased the $\mathsf{p H}$ of the solution to alkaline conditions, which negatively affected the removal of MB. Hu et al. [37] also found that $\mathbf{Cl}^{-}$ and ${\mathsf{C O}}_{3}^{-}$ in the water column had a very strong effect on the removal of TCEP by MIL-101 (Fe), and nearly no contaminants were removed after $60\mathrm{min}$ of reaction (Eqs. (13 and 14)). For persulphate system, Yin et al. [41] found that after adding $5\mathrm{\mM\HCO_{3}}^{-}$ and $\mathrm{PO}_{4}{}^{3-}$ , the degradation efficiency of SMX was only $20\%$ after $180\mathrm{min}$ by MIL-100(Fe)/PDS/vis system, whereas $\mathbf{Cl}^{-}$ and ${\mathrm{NO}}_{3}{}^{-}$ had almost no effect. Thus, the type of influence of the anion is different when different organic pollutants are removed by different methods.
